3
00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:43.447
I got a letter inviting
me to a college interview.

4
00:00:44.199 --> 00:00:46.491
from a college I didn't
remember applying to.

5
00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:49.385
And then I did remember writing an essay

6
00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:52.121
about confessing to
covering up a murder.

7
00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:55.958
I didn't mean to send
it. Somebody else did.

8
00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.550
And I got the interview.

9
00:00:58.379 --> 00:00:59.879
It's a crazy world. right?

10
00:01:07.222 --> 00:01:09.282
So. anyway. I have a
college interview today.

11
00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.934
- I have to go.
- Yeah.

12
00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:15.856
- I can't miss it.
- Well. I'll be sure to tell the doctor.

13
00:01:20.026 --> 00:01:22.276
I mean. I know I have
some marks on my record.

14
00:01:23.071 --> 00:01:25.738
and I've... I've had a lot of struggles.

15
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.290
but I guess my hope
would be to start over.

16
00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:33.412
You know. to be the person
that I know I can be.

17
00:01:33.414 --> 00:01:37.166
I think you'll find a lot of kids
at a school for the arts like ours

18
00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:39.798
have had challenging
high school experiences.

19
00:01:40.839 --> 00:01:42.922
And they come into their own in college.

20
00:01:42.924 --> 00:01:46.514
Yeah. I mean. like. there's more
to me that people don't know yet.

21
00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:50.096
- Your work is very good.
- Thank you.

22
00:01:50.098 --> 00:01:53.308
Tell me about the guns.
You make them look. um...

23
00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:57.729
elegant.

24
00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:00.823
I think guns can be beautiful.

25
00:02:01.651 --> 00:02:04.235
The way they look. along
with what they can do.

26
00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:05.237
It's...

27
00:02:06.197 --> 00:02:09.782
I mean. you can be attracted to them.

28
00:02:09.784 --> 00:02:10.914
Do you think that's...

29
00:02:12.078 --> 00:02:13.202
healthy?

30
00:02:13.204 --> 00:02:16.494
No. The fact that I put it in a picture

31
00:02:16.496 --> 00:02:19.125
doesn't mean I think it's a good thing.

32
00:02:19.127 --> 00:02:20.127
It's...

33
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.179
... it's a picture that
I needed to take.

34
00:02:26.384 --> 00:02:28.885
That I needed people to see.

35
00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:32.013
I'm actually... I'm scared of guns.

36
00:02:32.015 --> 00:02:35.385
And... and I think they're beautiful.

37
00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:39.613
You know? And I think a
lot of people talk about...

38
00:02:40.815 --> 00:02:45.065
kids are angry. kids are
sick. kids are violent.

39
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.572
But we don't talk about
the more complicated things

40
00:02:49.574 --> 00:02:52.994
like the fact that we
are attracted to guns.

41
00:02:53.828 --> 00:02:56.245
I mean. some people are
disgusted by them. for sure.

42
00:02:56.247 --> 00:03:00.208
But some of us are attracted.
like. drawn to them.

43
00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:04.065
And these pictures are
meant to get people thinking.

44
00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.920
you know. about why.

45
00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:11.387
... about the possibility of
self-harm more than anything.

46
00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:13.930
Are you?

47
00:03:13.932 --> 00:03:16.140
Concerned about the
possibility of self-harm?

48
00:03:16.142 --> 00:03:18.392
I think it's not a bad idea

49
00:03:18.394 --> 00:03:21.604
that we continue observation
for a period of time.

50
00:03:21.606 --> 00:03:22.980
From the police reports.

51
00:03:22.982 --> 00:03:26.442
it does appear that some sort of
breakdown took place at the school.

52
00:03:26.444 --> 00:03:28.736
The drill was incredibly stressful.

53
00:03:28.738 --> 00:03:29.988
and not just for Clay.

54
00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.384
Hey.

55
00:03:46.506 --> 00:03:48.046
How do you feel?

56
00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.386
They're gonna keep me here. aren't they?

57
00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:54.388
Yeah.

58
00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.659
I was arguing about it with them.

59
00:03:57.661 --> 00:03:59.850
I was... I was yelling
about it a minute ago.

60
00:04:01.271 --> 00:04:02.441
So I guess...

61
00:04:04.315 --> 00:04:07.525
congrats. You are full-on the good son.

62
00:04:07.527 --> 00:04:09.110
Dude. come...

63
00:04:09.112 --> 00:04:10.282
Come on. man.

64
00:04:12.073 --> 00:04:13.656
I'm sorry.

65
00:04:13.658 --> 00:04:15.158
I'm sorry that...

66
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.080
that I haven't been there to help you.

67
00:04:20.623 --> 00:04:22.463
I'm sorry that shit's so wrong.

68
00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:26.249
I'm not crazy.

69
00:04:29.257 --> 00:04:30.627
I'm just scared.

70
00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:32.675
Yeah. man.

71
00:04:32.677 --> 00:04:35.803
It's troubling. but I do think
we have to trust the process.

72
00:04:35.805 --> 00:04:36.805
I am too.

73
00:04:38.725 --> 00:04:41.500
Do you. uh. want me
to stay with you today?

74
00:04:41.502 --> 00:04:42.601
No.

75
00:04:42.603 --> 00:04:46.355
I know a doctor you
can stay in close touch with

76
00:04:46.357 --> 00:04:47.857
until his release.

77
00:04:47.859 --> 00:04:48.939
I'm kind of...

78
00:04:52.238 --> 00:04:53.318
embarrassed.

79
00:04:56.326 --> 00:04:58.534
- Good morning. sunshine.
- Hi.

80
00:04:58.536 --> 00:05:01.203
Dad. we talked about "sunshine".

81
00:05:01.205 --> 00:05:04.123
See. classic Clay. He's fine.

82
00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:06.250
The doctors would feel more comfortable

83
00:05:06.252 --> 00:05:11.714
if they kept an eye on you for
just a little while longer. Okay?

84
00:05:11.716 --> 00:05:13.591
"Okay". as in I get a vote?

85
00:05:13.593 --> 00:05:16.683
We'll get you out
of here as soon as we can.

86
00:05:21.893 --> 00:05:24.023
I gotta figure out what's up with Clay.

87
00:05:24.896 --> 00:05:26.062
People are blaming me

88
00:05:26.064 --> 00:05:30.441
like I had something to do with
this drill. It's crazy.

89
00:05:30.443 --> 00:05:33.152
No one thinks you had
anything to do with that drill.

90
00:05:33.154 --> 00:05:35.488
Or that crazy motherfucker Clay.

91
00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.910
Hey. don't call him crazy.

92
00:05:38.159 --> 00:05:39.867
I'm sorry.

93
00:05:39.869 --> 00:05:41.118
Just come back to bed.

94
00:05:42.914 --> 00:05:45.664
Hey. where you at?

95
00:05:45.666 --> 00:05:47.124
- Huh?
- What?

96
00:05:52.256 --> 00:05:54.465
Mm.

97
00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:56.258
Oh. my God.

98
00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.810
That Latin lover thing
is such a trope. Diego.

99
00:05:59.722 --> 00:06:01.272
It... The what now?

100
00:06:04.435 --> 00:06:06.185
- Oh. you really don't know?
- No.

101
00:06:07.897 --> 00:06:09.730
You're so pretty.

102
00:06:09.732 --> 00:06:11.690
Hello?

103
00:06:11.692 --> 00:06:14.777
Oh. shit! I. uh... I forgot
that Ani's back today.

104
00:06:14.779 --> 00:06:15.986
- Achola?
- Yep. yep.

105
00:06:15.988 --> 00:06:18.114
She lives here sometimes.
You gotta get out of here.

106
00:06:18.116 --> 00:06:19.490
- Come on.
- What? I got no clothes.

107
00:06:19.492 --> 00:06:21.742
Here. just come on. go.

108
00:06:21.744 --> 00:06:22.910
- Go!
- I got no clothes!

109
00:06:22.912 --> 00:06:26.372
Go! Get dressed on your
way out! Go! Oh. sorry!

110
00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:31.460
- Good morning.
- Hi! Welcome back.

111
00:06:34.549 --> 00:06:36.549
I think Jessica Davis knows.

112
00:06:37.343 --> 00:06:39.051
See. look here.

113
00:06:39.053 --> 00:06:42.680
Monty and someone are writing
back and forth using a number.

114
00:06:42.682 --> 00:06:45.015
"Twenty-one basically told me he did it.

115
00:06:45.017 --> 00:06:48.647
Twenty-one. using the
drugs Bryce gave him".

116
00:06:50.231 --> 00:06:51.361
So I guessed.

117
00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.730
What if that's a jersey number?

118
00:06:57.405 --> 00:06:58.405
Twenty-one.

119
00:07:00.116 --> 00:07:01.116
Twenty-one.

120
00:07:02.827 --> 00:07:03.827
Justin Foley.

121
00:07:06.456 --> 00:07:09.536
Diego is gonna try to
get it out of Zach today.

122
00:07:10.626 --> 00:07:13.335
And you think Jessica knows?

123
00:07:13.337 --> 00:07:14.795
She has to.

124
00:07:14.797 --> 00:07:17.006
I don't think she would lie to me.

125
00:07:17.008 --> 00:07:19.925
- To protect her boyfriend?
- I just...

126
00:07:19.927 --> 00:07:21.597
I thought we were friends.

127
00:07:23.306 --> 00:07:24.972
Me and her.

128
00:07:30.646 --> 00:07:33.564
Bolan thinks it was
more than the lockdown.

129
00:07:33.566 --> 00:07:35.106
He's still under observation.

130
00:07:37.069 --> 00:07:41.614
They did an initial evaluation.
and he's not psychotic.

131
00:07:41.616 --> 00:07:45.242
So they're in crisis management
to see if they need to commit him.

132
00:07:45.244 --> 00:07:47.286
They don't think he needs inpatient?

133
00:07:47.288 --> 00:07:48.954
Don't know yet.

134
00:07:48.956 --> 00:07:52.666
And I don't know if it's
just about the drill. or...

135
00:07:52.668 --> 00:07:55.798
- Well. what else would it be about?
- Well...

136
00:07:57.340 --> 00:08:00.633
I've been wanting to ask you a
few things about the Walker case.

137
00:08:00.635 --> 00:08:01.885
The Walker case?

138
00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.260
Yeah. I'm just...

139
00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:07.389
dotting the I's and all that.

140
00:08:07.391 --> 00:08:09.311
Making sure we have the whole picture.

141
00:08:10.144 --> 00:08:12.401
And since there's no audio or video

142
00:08:12.403 --> 00:08:14.772
from the Achola girl's statement.

143
00:08:14.774 --> 00:08:17.650
I was hoping you could help
me out with a few questions.

144
00:08:17.652 --> 00:08:18.652
Yeah.

145
00:08:19.612 --> 00:08:21.403
The officers subdued him.

146
00:08:21.405 --> 00:08:23.489
Clay had a gun in his hand!

147
00:08:23.491 --> 00:08:25.074
They beat the shit out of him.

148
00:08:25.076 --> 00:08:27.368
Jessica. Clay was violently upset.

149
00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:29.260
He was not coherent. and he was armed.

150
00:08:29.262 --> 00:08:30.538
The officers had to respond.

151
00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.498
We were all violently upset.

152
00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.000
We were fucking terrified!

153
00:08:35.002 --> 00:08:37.702
Right. The intent of the drill

154
00:08:37.704 --> 00:08:40.130
was to evaluate student
and staff response

155
00:08:40.132 --> 00:08:41.674
to an actual crisis.

156
00:08:41.676 --> 00:08:42.886
Whatever the intent was.

157
00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:45.719
the response is that we
were fucking freaked out.

158
00:08:45.721 --> 00:08:48.013
And now we're pissed off. Everyone is.

159
00:08:48.015 --> 00:08:50.345
I thought you and I agreed
safety was the priority.

160
00:08:51.352 --> 00:08:54.482
Do you really think
that Clay is safer now?

161
00:08:55.773 --> 00:08:57.193
I'm sorry about Clay.

162
00:08:58.234 --> 00:08:59.404
I really am.

163
00:09:07.577 --> 00:09:12.117
But I think there's more going
on there than just a lockdown.

164
00:09:20.256 --> 00:09:23.466
There's a petition going around
saying that I should resign.

165
00:09:25.553 --> 00:09:28.596
That I wanted this crazy drill.

166
00:09:28.598 --> 00:09:32.308
and the cameras. and
the metal detectors.

167
00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.227
Nobody knows about our conversations.

168
00:09:35.229 --> 00:09:37.399
But they know that I haven't spoken up.

169
00:09:38.357 --> 00:09:39.567
Do you think you should?

170
00:09:40.401 --> 00:09:41.401
Speak up?

171
00:09:42.403 --> 00:09:44.863
Do you think it would make
things better or worse?

172
00:09:48.701 --> 00:09:51.041
You know. they asked me at
my interview this morning...

173
00:09:54.165 --> 00:09:56.790
They asked me. "What's the
most stressful situation

174
00:09:56.792 --> 00:09:58.632
you've faced in your time here?"

175
00:10:00.921 --> 00:10:03.339
Of all the things I could have said.

176
00:10:03.341 --> 00:10:05.301
all the fucked-up shit that's happened.

177
00:10:06.761 --> 00:10:09.971
you know what I thought of?

178
00:10:11.807 --> 00:10:12.807
You.

179
00:10:14.935 --> 00:10:16.055
You and Clay.

180
00:10:18.105 --> 00:10:21.315
Wondering if my friends are
really just that: friends.

181
00:10:21.317 --> 00:10:24.379
Wondering if I'm gonna lose them or...

182
00:10:24.381 --> 00:10:26.403
or if they're gonna give up on me.

183
00:10:28.783 --> 00:10:29.865
I guess I know now.

184
00:10:29.867 --> 00:10:31.950
No one's giving up on you. Tyler.

185
00:10:31.952 --> 00:10:35.162
But what is going on? Why
were you shopping for guns?

186
00:10:35.164 --> 00:10:38.040
Do you think the last year.
everything we've been through.

187
00:10:38.042 --> 00:10:40.501
does that all just mean nothing to you?

188
00:10:40.503 --> 00:10:43.087
Do you think I can. just like that.
just go back to where I was.

189
00:10:43.089 --> 00:10:48.008
just where I was before you guys
all reached out and helped me?

190
00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.140
Before I worked so hard to get better?

191
00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.722
- You think all of that can just go away?
- I hope not.

192
00:10:53.724 --> 00:10:55.182
Then why go through my stuff?

193
00:10:55.184 --> 00:10:57.267
I was doing what I thought
was the right thing.

194
00:10:57.269 --> 00:11:00.939
You could have ruined my life.

195
00:11:05.569 --> 00:11:06.569
Hey.

196
00:11:07.363 --> 00:11:10.413
Winston said you guys bonded
during the lockdown yesterday.

197
00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.118
Mostly just got stoned.

198
00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.745
No. he said you got
some shit off your chest.

199
00:11:16.747 --> 00:11:18.617
Some very interesting shit.

200
00:11:23.796 --> 00:11:24.962
The fuck do you want?

201
00:11:24.964 --> 00:11:26.304
Tell me the story.

202
00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.798
Sounds like you've already heard it.

203
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.180
I think you're protecting one
of your friends. Like Clay is.

204
00:11:34.869 --> 00:11:37.119
You saw how that turned
out for him. right?

205
00:11:39.353 --> 00:11:43.188
You know. you're supposed to
be. like. this big stand-up guy.

206
00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:44.857
and you're keeping that secret?

207
00:11:44.859 --> 00:11:46.529
That's fucked up. Dempsey.

208
00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:51.160
Yeah. that's... that's worse
than anything any other guy did.

209
00:11:52.742 --> 00:11:54.542
Come on. man. Just come clean.

210
00:11:55.619 --> 00:11:56.619
Cleanse your soul.

211
00:11:57.621 --> 00:12:00.211
Or... pay the price.

212
00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:03.840
You've always been able to
talk. Diego. You know that?

213
00:12:05.129 --> 00:12:07.212
But when it comes time to play.

214
00:12:07.214 --> 00:12:08.634
the talk don't mean shit.

215
00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:10.650
Oh. yeah?

216
00:12:10.652 --> 00:12:11.652
Hmm.

217
00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:14.928
We'll see.

218
00:12:23.522 --> 00:12:25.482
Justin. I really gotta go.

219
00:12:29.695 --> 00:12:31.855
How was this morning? Are you okay?

220
00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:33.990
No.

221
00:12:35.242 --> 00:12:36.292
How's Clay?

222
00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.290
He's not okay.

223
00:12:41.624 --> 00:12:42.674
Nothing is.

224
00:12:45.252 --> 00:12:47.372
Zach told Winston that he beat up Bryce.

225
00:12:48.631 --> 00:12:49.761
Fuck! Uh...

226
00:12:50.674 --> 00:12:53.342
- What?
- Winston told Diego.

227
00:12:53.344 --> 00:12:56.178
So you're... you're still seeing Diego?

228
00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.597
He's. like. on a damn mission. I...

229
00:12:58.599 --> 00:13:01.141
I can't just drop him.
I have to handle shit.

230
00:13:01.143 --> 00:13:03.816
Okay. but is that all this
is? It's just you handling him.

231
00:13:03.818 --> 00:13:05.103
or whatever?

232
00:13:05.105 --> 00:13:06.105
Yes.

233
00:13:13.364 --> 00:13:14.364
Help.

234
00:13:15.866 --> 00:13:17.156
Ple... Please help.

235
00:13:19.119 --> 00:13:21.203
What? What is it?

236
00:13:21.205 --> 00:13:23.038
I shit the bed.

237
00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.040
Oh. man.

238
00:13:25.125 --> 00:13:27.084
I'm sorry. Uh. hold on.

239
00:13:27.086 --> 00:13:29.878
- Please?
- Yeah. hold on.

240
00:13:31.173 --> 00:13:33.090
Okay. we'll get you in the shower.

241
00:13:33.092 --> 00:13:34.411
I can't leave you alone.

242
00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:36.852
so I will wait until you've
finished your business.

243
00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:39.890
Oh. man. what a mess.

244
00:13:59.076 --> 00:14:01.618
We need some sheets in here.

245
00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.620
Taylor?

246
00:14:04.874 --> 00:14:07.844
You gotta crack the door. man.
I have to be able to hear you.

247
00:14:09.295 --> 00:14:10.544
Taylor?

248
00:14:10.546 --> 00:14:11.546
Anyone?

249
00:14:43.746 --> 00:14:44.826
He left?

250
00:14:47.917 --> 00:14:49.416
You mean he escaped?

251
00:14:49.418 --> 00:14:50.834
Yes.

252
00:14:50.836 --> 00:14:53.006
- How?
- Still unclear.

253
00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:58.220
Justin. I know that
Clay and I have history.

254
00:14:59.303 --> 00:15:00.802
but I am still here for him.

255
00:15:00.804 --> 00:15:01.814
And I'm worried.

256
00:15:03.015 --> 00:15:05.724
He's in a fragile mental state.

257
00:15:05.726 --> 00:15:08.595
Yeah. you can thank Bolan for that.

258
00:15:08.597 --> 00:15:11.480
It's not safe for him
to be alone right now.

259
00:15:11.482 --> 00:15:13.523
He could act out violently.

260
00:15:13.525 --> 00:15:14.942
