Tony said I could stay.

404
00:23:40.511 --> 00:23:41.931
You don't have to.

405
00:23:43.285 --> 00:23:44.285
I do.

406
00:23:49.833 --> 00:23:51.043
What I did...

407
00:23:53.336 --> 00:23:54.706
... with Bryce...

408
00:23:58.758 --> 00:24:00.178
was unforgivable.

409
00:24:03.722 --> 00:24:07.602
And I'm so sorry that I hurt you.

410
00:24:08.685 --> 00:24:09.845
I didn't mean to.

411
00:24:10.937 --> 00:24:11.937
I didn't.

412
00:24:13.023 --> 00:24:16.316
I wasn't thinking. Full stop.

413
00:24:16.318 --> 00:24:19.278
I was just being a stupid kid.

414
00:24:23.325 --> 00:24:25.035
It's just...

415
00:24:25.869 --> 00:24:27.199
All I know is that...

416
00:24:29.664 --> 00:24:31.084
I guess that I was lonely.

417
00:24:34.169 --> 00:24:36.509
And I didn't think
about the consequences.

418
00:24:40.258 --> 00:24:42.178
I think girls do that sometimes.

419
00:24:44.471 --> 00:24:45.601
With boys.

420
00:24:54.397 --> 00:24:56.527
I worry that things have...

421
00:24:57.734 --> 00:24:59.444
... completely fallen apart...

422
00:25:01.738 --> 00:25:02.738
with you and me.

423
00:25:05.242 --> 00:25:06.332
And everything.

424
00:25:11.706 --> 00:25:13.957
And the only thing that's clear is

425
00:25:13.959 --> 00:25:16.459
that I'm not the person
to put them back together.

426
00:25:39.276 --> 00:25:40.646
Is that a Rickenbacker?

427
00:25:42.362 --> 00:25:43.653
Guild.

428
00:25:43.655 --> 00:25:44.985
Starfire III.

429
00:25:46.116 --> 00:25:47.696
1966.

430
00:25:57.752 --> 00:26:00.545
This time. you take the
couch. I take the chair.

431
00:26:00.547 --> 00:26:01.547
Clay.

432
00:26:03.008 --> 00:26:05.132
It's fine if you want to feel powerful

433
00:26:05.134 --> 00:26:07.093
at this moment. I understand that.

434
00:26:07.095 --> 00:26:10.179
But at some point. I have
to involve the authorities.

435
00:26:10.181 --> 00:26:12.431
You take the couch. I take the chair.

436
00:26:32.704 --> 00:26:35.038
You don't want the chair after all?

437
00:26:35.040 --> 00:26:37.874
I'm supposed to go to a
college interview tomorrow.

438
00:26:37.876 --> 00:26:40.376
You believe that? A college interview.

439
00:26:40.378 --> 00:26:42.170
And you don't feel ready for that?

440
00:26:42.172 --> 00:26:44.088
I can't just sit there and talk.

441
00:26:44.090 --> 00:26:46.507
I can't even hold still anymore.

442
00:26:46.509 --> 00:26:48.217
Why do you think that is?

443
00:26:48.219 --> 00:26:49.969
It started when I was arrested.

444
00:26:51.348 --> 00:26:55.183
When they moved me from the
sheriff's station to the county jail.

445
00:26:55.185 --> 00:26:57.826
They had me in handcuffs and leg irons.

446
00:26:57.828 --> 00:26:59.228
and they shut me in the back of the van.

447
00:26:59.230 --> 00:27:00.900
No windows. no air. just dark.

448
00:27:02.567 --> 00:27:04.067
Must have been terrifying.

449
00:27:06.321 --> 00:27:10.323
And you felt confined
today. at the hospital?

450
00:27:10.325 --> 00:27:12.241
I just... I had to get out.

451
00:27:12.243 --> 00:27:13.618
Get away. I...

452
00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:15.828
From people who were trying to help you?

453
00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:17.460
I... I just felt afraid.

454
00:27:19.668 --> 00:27:23.958
I've felt so afraid of so
many things for so long.

455
00:27:26.216 --> 00:27:29.592
I mean. I don't even think I can
ever remember not being afraid.

456
00:27:29.594 --> 00:27:30.802
Try.

457
00:27:30.804 --> 00:27:32.184
Try to tell me...

458
00:27:33.765 --> 00:27:35.932
about a time you felt safe.

459
00:27:35.934 --> 00:27:37.100
Taken care of.

460
00:27:37.102 --> 00:27:38.142
I...

461
00:27:39.229 --> 00:27:41.187
I don't know. I don't know.

462
00:27:41.189 --> 00:27:43.229
Go as far back as you need to.

463
00:27:59.249 --> 00:28:01.419
I remember this time I was. like.

464
00:28:02.502 --> 00:28:04.712
seven. I think. or eight.

465
00:28:06.631 --> 00:28:09.381
And I had this crazy fever.

466
00:28:10.385 --> 00:28:12.295
like things didn't feel real.

467
00:28:13.388 --> 00:28:15.808
And my dad stayed home
and took care of me.

468
00:28:17.183 --> 00:28:21.653
And I slept on the
couch with our dog. um...

469
00:28:22.689 --> 00:28:23.819
who was. like...

470
00:28:25.483 --> 00:28:27.443
It was like she was guarding me.

471
00:28:29.571 --> 00:28:31.446
And I remember waking up

472
00:28:31.448 --> 00:28:33.988
and my dad was sitting there.

473
00:28:35.034 --> 00:28:36.034
just...

474
00:28:38.329 --> 00:28:41.329
sort of stroking the hair on my head.

475
00:28:46.129 --> 00:28:47.129
And...

476
00:28:49.048 --> 00:28:50.878
he looked so worried. but I...

477
00:28:53.261 --> 00:28:54.511
I didn't feel worried.

478
00:28:57.640 --> 00:28:59.140
I just felt glad he was there.

479
00:29:01.811 --> 00:29:03.651
Why do you think your parents worry?

480
00:29:06.733 --> 00:29:09.243
I don't... I don't want them to.

481
00:29:10.028 --> 00:29:11.648
But why do you think they do?

482
00:29:12.572 --> 00:29:13.572
Because of...

483
00:29:14.949 --> 00:29:16.909
everything I do. Because of the...

484
00:29:17.744 --> 00:29:20.745
the trouble I've caused.
Because I'm not right. I mean...

485
00:29:20.747 --> 00:29:23.457
Do you think if you were
perfect. they'd never worry...

486
00:29:25.376 --> 00:29:29.086
about where you were. what you
were doing. if you were healthy?

487
00:29:30.298 --> 00:29:31.838
Happy? Safe?

488
00:29:35.595 --> 00:29:37.428
I guess they would.

489
00:29:37.430 --> 00:29:39.055
Then when they do.

490
00:29:39.057 --> 00:29:41.182
can you try to remember that feeling

491
00:29:41.184 --> 00:29:42.814
of being glad they're there?

492
00:29:44.395 --> 00:29:45.685
I can try. Yeah.

493
00:29:46.606 --> 00:29:47.976
Then perhaps...

494
00:29:49.025 --> 00:29:52.945
you can start to believe that
there are people in your life...

495
00:29:54.864 --> 00:29:56.414
that wanna take care of you.

496
00:29:57.909 --> 00:29:59.949
That want you to do well.

497
00:30:03.206 --> 00:30:06.666
Parents. teachers. doctors.

498
00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:10.670
Even college interviewers.

499
00:30:13.466 --> 00:30:14.466
I can try.

500
00:30:20.431 --> 00:30:22.391
Sweetheart.

501
00:30:25.937 --> 00:30:27.979
I've spoken with Sheriff Diaz.

502
00:30:27.981 --> 00:30:30.189
and I don't think Clay
is at risk of self-harm.

503
00:30:30.191 --> 00:30:31.441
He can go home.

504
00:30:32.193 --> 00:30:35.953
He and I have decided it's
best I see him twice a week

505
00:30:36.823 --> 00:30:38.281
for the next while.

506
00:30:38.283 --> 00:30:39.283
Thank you.

507
00:30:40.785 --> 00:30:43.865
Do you want to sleep in the house
tonight instead of out back?

508
00:30:45.540 --> 00:30:46.914
Is Justin home?

509
00:30:46.916 --> 00:30:47.916
Yeah.

510
00:30:49.460 --> 00:30:50.460
Then I'll be fine.

511
00:30:51.963 --> 00:30:52.963
Okay.

512
00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:01.220
Okay.

513
00:31:40.219 --> 00:31:41.878
They say that resiliency

514
00:31:41.880 --> 00:31:43.899
is the truest predictor of success.

515
00:31:47.435 --> 00:31:49.268
Do they say that?

516
00:31:49.270 --> 00:31:50.270
Mm-hmm.

517
00:31:52.273 --> 00:31:53.273
Huh.

518
00:31:56.027 --> 00:31:58.847
But isn't resiliency just

519
00:31:58.849 --> 00:32:01.948
one more way of saying that
we should cope with things

520
00:32:01.950 --> 00:32:03.740
rather than trying to change them?

521
00:32:04.726 --> 00:32:05.826
I. um...

522
00:32:05.828 --> 00:32:07.998
And what does real change look like?

523
00:32:15.922 --> 00:32:18.512
I. um... I had two friends.

524
00:32:19.801 --> 00:32:21.926
Two very different friends.

525
00:32:21.928 --> 00:32:24.178
Two people I love...

526
00:32:26.557 --> 00:32:27.927
who each had a moment...

527
00:32:29.394 --> 00:32:33.104
in their lives when they
looked in their world

528
00:32:33.106 --> 00:32:36.146
and saw that nothing
was ever gonna change.

529
00:32:37.402 --> 00:32:38.402
Ever.

530
00:32:39.445 --> 00:32:41.275
And they each made a decision...

531
00:32:42.740 --> 00:32:44.080
in that one moment.

532
00:32:45.660 --> 00:32:46.700
One...

533
00:32:48.830 --> 00:32:49.870
terrible.

534
00:32:51.624 --> 00:32:53.334
painful decision...

535
00:32:56.212 --> 00:32:58.302
that they could never take back.

536
00:33:05.805 --> 00:33:08.215
And that's what brought the change.

537
00:33:11.728 --> 00:33:12.768
Painful...

538
00:33:14.480 --> 00:33:15.480
awful...

539
00:33:16.315 --> 00:33:17.355
change.

540
00:33:19.068 --> 00:33:21.110
Change is never easy.

541
00:33:23.448 --> 00:33:24.448
No.

542
00:33:25.783 --> 00:33:27.203
No. no. it isn't.

543
00:33:28.995 --> 00:33:30.245
Thank you for that.

544
00:33:36.461 --> 00:33:39.039
Um. I'm sorry to pull you
out of class like this. buddy.

545
00:33:39.041 --> 00:33:40.421
